Z||000000||JetroGT||06-17-2001||06:04 AM||||I'm in the second year of restoring my blue GT. I've come a long way so far. Here are some before and after shots.<P>See how it's tilted like that? Bad engine mounts and tranny mounts. $$$<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87engine0.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/s87engine1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Engine3.jpg"> <P><BR>Now I'm working on the suspension. I just replaced the upper and lower control arms in the front. That fixed my drifting and rattling problems on the highway. Next is to replace the colum switch and repaint the rear wing. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT-maniac||06-17-2001||12:37 PM||||Well your engine seems to be really coming along. Looks like you got the motor mounts fixed. Now you just need some red plug wires ( I used taylor spiro pro's on mine ) and an EGR valve cover. I paid a dollar for mine from a wrecker though I've seen them going for over twenty on Ebay ! Crazy, I should start selling them myself..||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnmac||06-17-2001||06:33 PM||||Looks like you and I are doing the same thing.<P>I am also in my 2nd year of restoration per my 86 GT - - which I stole for $500.<P>Based on what I have done:<BR>Replace your EGR and get some aluminunized heat resistant paint for the heat shields.<P>I am also presently redoing my rear suspension. Bought rebuilt tranaxles from Autozone and completely redoing every suspension component.<P>Be glad to exchange stories with you.<P>This is my first car restoration in 20 years and this Fiero is a *****  to work on some times to say the least. The Fiero guys and especially this forum is excellant.<P>Take care,<P>John<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierofrek||06-17-2001||07:32 PM||||WOW, you did a wonderful job on the engine! a complete 180 degrees!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
